<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">5 December in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 5 December, from 63 BCE to 1933.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/catiline" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/catiline.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/63-bce">63 BCE</a> <span class="tih-ago">2,088 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Senate condemns Catiline's fellow conspirators</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cicero">Cicero</a>'s fourth speech against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catiline">Catiline</a>, and Cato's demand for severity, the Senate voted to execute five conspirators without trial. Cicero was hailed as saviour of the Republic but later exiled for it.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/633">633 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,393 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Fourth Council of Toledo opens under Isidore of Seville</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">All the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania">Hispania</a> gathered at the church of Saint Leocadia in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toledo">Toledo</a> for the council convened by the Visigothic king Sisenand, over which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isidore-of-seville">Isidore of Seville</a> probably presided. It decreed a uniform liturgy throughout the kingdom.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isidore-of-seville">Isidore of Seville</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1033 CE <span class="tih-ago">993 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">An earthquake in the Jordan Rift Valley devastates the Levant</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">An earthquake in the Jordan Rift Valley, estimated at above magnitude 7.0, caused extreme devastation across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/levant">Levant</a> and a tsunami along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> coast. At least 70,000 people were killed.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/levant">Levant</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1360">1360 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">666 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John II creates the first franc</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">By an ordinance issued at Compiègne, the newly released <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-ii-of-france">John II of France</a> created the gold franc, partly to raise his ransom. The franc remained the name of French currency until the euro.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1484">1484 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">542 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pope Innocent VIII issues a bull against witchcraft</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The bull Summis desiderantes affectibus authorised the inquisitors Heinrich Kramer and Jacob Sprenger to pursue witches in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. Kramer printed it with his Malleus Maleficarum, fuelling later witch hunts.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1757">1757 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">269 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Frederick the Great routs an Austrian army at Leuthen</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">West of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wroclaw">Breslau</a> in Silesia, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-the-great">Frederick the Great</a> used the oblique order of attack to rout an Austrian army about twice the size of his own under Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-duke-of-lower-lorraine">Charles of Lorraine</a>. The victory restored Prussian control of Silesia.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-leuthen">Battle of Leuthen</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-the-great">Frederick the Great</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seven-years-war">Seven Years' War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1791">1791 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">235 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mozart dies in Vienna aged 35</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wolfgang-amadeus-mozart">Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart</a> died after a short illness, leaving his Requiem unfinished. In a career of barely three decades he wrote more than 600 works, including The Marriage of Figaro and The Magic Flute.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1933">1933 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">93 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Prohibition ends in the United States</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/utah">Utah</a> became the 36th state to ratify the 21st Amendment, repealing national Prohibition. The ban on alcohol had lasted almost 14 years and fed a boom in organised crime.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 5 December <span class="n">7</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/pope-julius-ii"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pope-julius-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Pope Julius II</span><span class="tp">1443–1513</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/fausto-sozzini"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/fausto-sozzini.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Fausto Sozzini</span><span class="tp">1539–1604</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/george-armstrong-custer"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/george-armstrong-custer.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">George Armstrong Custer</span><span class="tp">1839–1876</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jozef-pilsudski"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jozef-pilsudski.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Józef Piłsudski</span><span class="tp">1867–1935</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/c-r-swart"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/c-r-swart.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">C. R. Swart</span><span class="tp">1894–1982</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/anastasio-somoza-debayle"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/anastasio-somoza-debayle.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Anastasio Somoza Debayle</span><span class="tp">1925–1980</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/bhumibol-adulyadej"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/bhumibol-adulyadej.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Bhumibol Adulyadej</span><span class="tp">1927–2016</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 5 December <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/pierre-gaultier-de-varennes-sieur-de-la-verendrye"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pierre-gaultier-de-varennes-sieur-de-la-verendrye.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Pierre Gaultier de Varennes, sieur de La Vérendrye</span><span class="tp">1685–1749</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/wolfgang-amadeus-mozart"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/wolfgang-amadeus-mozart.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart</span><span class="tp">1756–1791</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ne-win"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ne-win.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ne Win</span><span class="tp">1911–2002</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/nelson-mandela"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/nelson-mandela.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Nelson Mandela</span><span class="tp">1918–2013</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/michael-i-of-romania"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/michael-i-of-romania.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Michael I of Romania</span><span class="tp">1921–2017</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
